sequenceDiagram
    participant Platform as Platform Operator (mTLS client)
    participant Proxy as Reverse Proxy (Caddy/Traefik/nginx)
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (<gateId>)
    participant Auth as PlatformAuthChecker
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over Platform: Platform's eDelivery AP cert subject DN<br/>has been registered against TWO active rows in `platforms`<br/>(typically operator misconfiguration: one platform was<br/>renamed and the old row was not soft-deleted).

    Platform->>+Proxy: POST /v1/identifiers/550e8400-...<br/>Client cert: CN=eDelivery-Platform, O=<orgName>
    Proxy->>Proxy: Validate cert chain against MS-issued CA
    Proxy->>+Gate: POST /v1/identifiers/550e8400-...<br/>X-Client-Cert-Subject: CN=eDelivery-Platform, O=<orgName><br/>X-Client-Cert-Serial: 0123456789ABCDEF

    Gate->>+Auth: resolvePlatform(certSubject, certSerial)
    Auth->>+DB: Resolve active platforms rows by (cert_subject, cert_serial)
    DB-->>-Auth: 2 active platforms match: '<platformA>', '<platformB>'
    Auth->>Auth: matches > 1 → CONFIGURATION ERROR
    Auth-->>-Gate: ForbiddenException(FORBIDDEN_MULTI_PLATFORM)

    Gate-->>Proxy: 403 Forbidden<br/>{ "type": "https://api.efti.ee/errors/forbidden-multi-platform",<br/>  "code": "FORBIDDEN_MULTI_PLATFORM",<br/>  "title": "Certificate matches multiple active platforms",<br/>  "status": 403,<br/>  "detail": "The presented client certificate subject DN matches more than one active row in the platforms registry. This is a configuration error — exactly one platform per certificate. Contact the gate operator." }
    deactivate Gate
    Proxy-->>-Platform: 403 Forbidden (forwarded)

    Note over Platform,Gate: Resolution: gate operator soft-deletes the<br/>obsolete row (`is_active=FALSE`) so the cert resolves<br/>to exactly one active platform on the next call.

    Note over Platform: After fix:
    Platform->>+Gate: POST /v1/identifiers/550e8400-...<br/>X-Client-Cert-Subject: CN=eDelivery-Platform, O=<orgName>
    Gate->>+Auth: resolvePlatform(certSubject, certSerial)
    Auth->>+DB: Resolve active platforms rows by (cert_subject, cert_serial)
    DB-->>-Auth: 1 active platform matches: '<platformA>'
    Auth->>Auth: matches == 1 → OK
    Auth-->>-Gate: Platform{id="<platformA>"}
    Gate-->>-Platform: 200 OK
